Here is the root cause:
The bug occurs because the `DisjunctionSumScorer` was calling the `score()` method on a subscorer that had already returned `NO_MORE_DOCS`, leading to potential errors or unexpected behavior when attempting to score a non-existent document. This situation arises when the scoring logic does not properly check the state of the document iterator before invoking scoring methods.

